<title>GERMANY: Thyssen details 1995/96 results.</title>
<headline>Thyssen details 1995/96 results.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Sept 30,</p>
<p>1996: (in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   350     vs 775</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     654     vs 1,026</p>
<p>    Group income from ord. activities    611     vs 1,026</p>
<p>    Group equity				 5,850   vs 5,405</p>
<p>    Equity/assets ratio (percent)	  23	vs 21.6</p>
<p>    Return on equity (percent)		6	vs 14.3</p>
<p>    Investment				   2,429   vs 2,191</p>
<p>    Depreciation				 1,822   vs 1,846</p>
<p>    Cash flow				    2,189   vs 2,812</p>
<p>    Net financial debt			 3,862   vs 3,752</p>
<p>    Work force (annual average)	    123,746 vs 126,987</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     Germany				     93,629  vs 96,815</p>
<p>     Foreign				     30,117  vs 30,172</p>
<p>    Group sales				  38,673  vs 39,123</p>
<p>    Parent net profit			  350     vs 478</p>
<p>    Dividend				     8	 vs 10 marks</p>
<p>    Total dividend payment		   250     vs 313</p>
<p>The company gave the following details of its results adjusted according to the German financial analysts (DVFA/SG) accounting method.</p>
<p>    Net earnings per share		   16	vs 24 marks</p>
<p>    Gross earnings per share		 20	vs 28 marks</p>
<p>    Cash flow (DVFA per share)	     68	vs 89 marks</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German steel and engineering group is Thyssen AG.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
